<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/134011> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 134011 ;
    nex:description """Consumers are often motivated to engage in environmentally friendly consumption
practices. However, this is challenging, as it comes at an increased financial cost. The present
research argues that, while wanting to save money, frugal consumers are also conscious of
conserving resources from their consumption. Several studies present evidence that frugal
consumers will engage in environmentally friendly behaviors (e.g., spend to CO2 offset) when they
believe they first got a deal but also believe their consumption will be more harmful to the
environment. Evidence highlights the role of guilt in this case, where frugal consumers feel guiltier
than less frugal consumers under circumstances of saving money but inflicting more
environmental harm. This guilt then subsequently drives ethical consumption intentions, such as
CO2 offsetting of flights.""" ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2025 ;
    nex:title "The green premium paradox: balancing cost and sustainability in co2 offsetting for flights" .

