    nex:articleId 76495 ;
    nex:description "Landmined Landscapes are perceptional war scenarios based on guerrilla practices intended to deceive the enemy. The effectiveness of these particular landscapes rely on the uncertainty and anxiety created when an outsider is unable to distinguish if a landscape is an untouched wild space or if it is an explosive trap, perfectly arranged to appear wild. FARC methodically used this incertitude as the principal agency to deter the enemy from their areas." ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2021 ;
    nex:title "Landmined landscapes in Colombia as FARC guerrilla´s material culture" .

