<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/80787> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 80787 ;
    nex:description "Cyanobacteria (or blue-green algae) blooms occur in freshwater and saline ecosystems under certain environmental conditions, such as eutrophication. These blooms are often accompanied by cyanotoxins in the water, which are a health risk to animals and humans. Because the eutrophication of water bodies is becoming more frequent due to organic pollution pressure from swage discharge, blooms have become frequent and are often difficult to manage by communities affected by these phenomena in their water reservoirs." ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2021 ;
    nex:title "Bioaugmentation with a chlorophyte consortium controls harmful cyanobacterial bloom" .

