<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/107256> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 107256 ;
    nex:classification "A" ;
    nex:description "Earthen buildings are a fundamental part of Colombia's historical architectural heritage. This heritage has been deteriorating due to lack of knowledge, disconnection from cultural roots and because of the inherent structural vulnerability of these buildings, which is mainly caused by earthquakes and moisture. Throughout recent years, research has been carried out in order to structurally intervene and preserve these buildings, however, within the Colombian context, there are few studies regarding the location, distribution and main characteristics of earthen buildings, especially in urban environments. Therefore, this research is presented from general to specific, beginning with an approach to Andean earthen architecture in Colombia, and ending with a case study of earthen architecture within an urban environment: The Historic Centre of Bogotá (HCB). Based on this context, the most important earth construction techniques, rehabilitation techniques and their advances were identified. Regarding the urban HCB case analysed, it was posible to identify location, hierarchical relationships, geometric characteristics and intervention techniques of one- and two-storey earthen buildings, by means of a procedure that can be replicated in other Colombian cities. The relevance of analysing Colombian earthen constructions is to contribute to the development of intervention techniques in order to, firstly, facilitate the conservation of their architectural heritage characteristics, and secondly, to improve their structural behaviour." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/10104> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2023 ;
    nex:title "An approach to Colombian Andean Earthen Architecture in Urban Environments: A case study of Bogotá Historic Centre" ;
    nex:url "https://doi.org/10.1080/13556207.2022.2160556"^^xsd:anyURI .

