<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/108167> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 108167 ;
    nex:description """Abstract. The concept of stability has proved very useful in the field of Banach space geometry.
In this note we introduce and study a corresponding concept in the setting of Banach
algebras, which we call multiplicative stability. As we shall prove, various interesting
examples of Banach algebras are multiplicatively unstable, such as Fourier algebras over
non-compact amenable groups. We obtain generalizations of some results by Farah–Hart–
Sherman on stability in the model theoretical sense.""" ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/8219> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2022 ;
    nex:title """Multiplicative stability of Banach algebras. Joint work with Matthias Neufang. [Submitted to The Canadian Mathematical Bulletin  
Paper ID: 221022-Neufang.]""" .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/108168> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 108168 ;
    nex:description """Abstract. We establish the first criterion for a general Banach algebra to be left strongly Arens
irregular with a small DWe establish the first criterion for a general Banach algebra to be left strongly Arens
irregular with a small DTC set. We give a number of applications to algebras that
are central in abstract harmonic analysis, such as (weighted) group algebras, measure
algebras, and Fourier algebras. In particular, for large classes of topological groups, we
give an answer to an open problem raised by H.G. Dales.TC set. We give a number of applications to algebras that
are central in abstract harmonic analysis, such as (weighted) group algebras, measure
algebras, and Fourier algebras. In particular, for large classes of topological groups, we
give an answer to an open problem raised by H.G. Dales.""" ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/8219> ;
