<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/111659> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 111659 ;
    nex:classification "A" ;
    nex:description "This critique evaluates the use of the P-HENS software for developing recommended heat exchanger network designs compared to the commercial simulator Aspen Energy Analyzer. The similarities between the two software when carrying out an energy integration are discussed, as well as their advantages and possible improvements to be implemented in the tool." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/10151> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2023 ;
    nex:title "Critique – Comparison between P-HENS and Aspen Energy Analyzer for heat exchanger network synthesis" ;
    nex:url "http://doi.org/10.1016/j.ece.2023.02.004"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/111661> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 111661 ;
    nex:classification "B" ;
    nex:description "El oleoducto es uno de los medios de transporte de hidrocarburos más seguros y rentables. Sin embargo, las liberaciones de hidrocarburos y los posteriores incendios y explosiones, se presentan como eventos persistentes. La evaluación cuantitativa de riesgos (QRA) permite abordar el riesgo y prevenir estos eventos. En este sentido, se han propuesto diferentes enfoques para los oleoductos, pero pocos estudios se centran en el transporte de petróleo. Este artículo presenta una metodología para realizar QRA para oleoductos terrestres, que se basa en el cálculo de indicadores de riesgo individuales y sociales. Esta metodología se ilustra utilizando un caso de estudio auténtico de un segmento de 17,53 km de longitud de un oleoducto terrestre ubicado en el suroccidente de Colombia, considerando escenarios de jet y pool fire.−4 y 8,52 × 10 −5 año −1 , respectivamente. El IRPA para las personas cercanas a la tubería está entre 2,31 × 10 −4 y 2,60 × 10 −4 año −1 . El IRPA para los trabajadores es tolerable, mientras que para las personas puede clasificarse como inaceptable. El riesgo social se representó mediante la curva F-N, lo que indica que el riesgo es inaceptable y que las poblaciones cercanas podrían reubicarse." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/9910> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2023 ;
    nex:title "Evaluación cuantitativa de riesgos de oleoductos terrestres en escenarios de incendio y explosión" ;
    nex:url "http://doi.org/10.3390/pr11020557"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/111662> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 111662 ;
    nex:classification "A" ;
    nex:description "Cupuassu (Theobroma grandiflorum) is an Amazonian fruit with high nutritional value and considerable antioxidant activity mainly due to phenolics and ascorbic acid. To preserve those compounds and their activity, the pulp of cupuassu was spray dried using inulin/maltodextrin mixtures as wall material. The process was optimized using response surface methodology (RSM) based on a central composite design, with inlet temperature (X1), inulin concentration in the wall material (X2) and wall material concentration (X3) as independent variables. Yield, moisture, water activity (aw), hygroscopicity, water solubility index (WSI), and ascorbic acid (AA) and phenolic (PC) encapsulation efficiency were studied. The fitted results (mostly second-order equations) enabled us to determine the optimal conditions of inlet temperature (185 °C), inulin concentration (44%), and wall material concentration (35%) with low predictive error and high desirability (close to 1.0). The microencapsulates with a sphere of diameter 2.16 ± 1.32 μm had a smooth surface and a low degree of agglomeration. Under simulated intestinal fluid conditions, 76.7% of ascorbic acid was released. These results suggest the great potential of the obtained cupuassu microencapsulates as a strategy for Amazonian fruit valorization." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/60561> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2023 ;
    nex:title "Optimization of the encapsulation process of Cupuassu (Theobroma grandiflorum) pulp by spray drying as an alternative for the valorization of Amazonian fruits" ;
    nex:url "http://doi.org/10.1016/j.lwt.2023.114994"^^xsd:anyURI .

