<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/114274> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 114274 ;
    nex:classification "D" ;
    nex:description "In this study solid-gas interactions during sintering of powder metallurgy (PM) irons are simulated by coupling mass, heat, and momentum phenomena in a non-stationary model. The consolidation of a PM compact requires the elimination of the nanometric oxides covering the particles. Theoretically this is achieved by adjusting the inlet atmosphere composition to guarantee thermodynamically reductive values at the processing temperature. That depends on the quotient of hydrogen and water partial pressures when N2/H2mixtures are employed. However the actual atmosphere composition inside the porous part is not easy to predict because water produced during reaction can locally increases the pH2O/pH2 value. This work proposes a methodology to study the effects of local atmosphere degradation on reduction times. The influence of compact temperature and external gas velocities during the processing of the iron/wüstite system was evaluated. © 2013 Universidad Simón Bolívar." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/9584> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2013 ;
    nex:title "Modeling reduction reactions during sintering of powder metallurgy irons" .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/114277> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 114277 ;
    nex:classification "B" ;
    nex:description "This paper describes the structural analysis by single crystal X-ray diffraction (SCXRD) of N-(4-methoxybenzyl)-L-tyrosine ethyl ester; a scorpion-like conformation was revealed between the ethoxycarbonyl group and the 4-hydroxyphenyl group. Zig-zag linear arrangements having head-to-tail intermolecular hydrogen bonds (O-H***N) were also observed between N-(4-methoxybenzyl)-l-tyrosine ethyl ester units. It was determined that this amine reacts with formaldehyde to form linear dimers, trimers, and tetramers made up of N-(4-methoxybenzyl)-l-tyrosine ethyl ester units linked by methylene bridges." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/43204> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2024 ;
    nex:title "N-(4-methoxybenzyl)-L-tyrosine ethyl ester: Synthesis, structural analysis, and reaction with formaldehyde" ;
    nex:url "http://doi.org/10.1016/j.molstruc.2023.137079"^^xsd:anyURI .

