<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/116796> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 116796 ;
    nex:description "This Systematic Literature Review (SLR) examines the integration of sustainable practices throughout the Material Life Cycle (MLC) to enhance Sustainable Construction (SC). Analyzing 97 articles, the study identifies three main trends: Circular Construction & Sustainable Waste Management, Sustainable Supply Chain and Life Cycle Assessment (LCA), and Carbon Neutral Construction & Renewable Energy Integration. It highlights the need for standardized methodologies across MLC stages, particularly in early integration, production, and decision-making. Significant gaps include a limited understanding of complex supply chain dynamics and effective management of supply networks. The review also notes a substantial increase in related research over the past five years, signaling growing interest in Circular Economy (CE) practices. However, the adoption of these practices is inconsistent, emphasizing the critical role of stakeholder engagement and integrated decision-making in achieving holistic sustainability. This SLR underscores the need for comprehensive strategies to advance SC, providing a foundation for future research and practical applications." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/84655> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2024 ;
    nex:title "Sustainable practices in the Material life-cycle: A systematic Review" .

