<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/117346> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 117346 ;
    nex:classification "B" ;
    nex:description "Book and media reviews in the Comparative Education Review (CER) have played an important role in the ongoing construction of the field. Reviews contribute to building connections and networks between comparative educators worldwide. They inject vitality into the field as different resources are shared, reflected upon, and critiqued. Finally, reviews are an essential resource for those teaching comparative and international education and practitioners in the field. This essay explores the history and evolution of reviews in the journal over the past 70 years. From this historical analysis, we generate some insights that inform our editorial approach moving forward." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/43236> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2024 ;
    nex:title "Seventy Years of Reviews in Comparative Education Review: Reflections on the Tradition and New Directions" ;
    nex:url "https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/abs/10.1086/728725"^^xsd:anyURI .

