<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/128961> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 128961 ;
    nex:description "Colombia ranks sixth among 24 countries in the Latin America and Caribbean region in the implementation of the 2030 Agenda. Despite its preferential position in the region, Colombia has not met any of the seventeen Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). In this context of Sustainable Development, emphasis is placed on SDG 4 on Quality Education, from which the research question is formulated: what were Colombia's results in the fulfillment of SDG 4 concerning the countries of Latin America and the Caribbean between 2019 and 2021? To answer it, this research design was guided by the positivist stance and was implemented through the non-experimental method of the causal case study. In the SDG Index between 2019 and 2021, Colombia has maintained a moderate level of progress at a rate above 50% of the expected trend in SDG 4, but below the necessary trajectory for the fulfillment of SDG 4 in 2030. Therefore, Colombia has a critical lag in SDG 4, with a medium risk of not meeting this SDG by 2030. © 2023 Latin American and Caribbean Consortium of Engineering Institutions. All rights reserved." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/9972> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2023 ;
    nex:title "SDG 4 on Quality Education in Colombia between 2019 and 2021" ;
    nex:url "https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85172363767&partnerID=40&md5=07626c2a0b1ee63cf051abad5f2901ed"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/128962> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 128962 ;
    nex:classification "C" ;
    nex:description "Este artículo identifica elementos de multifuncionalidad en la agricultura familiar y analiza sus interacciones y contribuciones en la adaptación de los sistemas productivos al cambio climático en zonas centrales andinas de Colombia. La investigación analiza quince fincas familiares de tres municipios Andinos de Colombia y sus sistemas productivos, en tres fases; en la primera, se realiza la caracterización de la agricultura familiar mediante la aplicación de un instrumento de recolección de información; en la segunda, se identifican y analizan los elementos de la multifuncionalidad a través de una cartografía social que permite georreferenciar las distintas funciones; y, en la tercera, se valora el aporte de la multifuncionalidad en la adaptación al cambio climático mediante indicadores específicos." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/9834> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2025 ;
    nex:title "Multifuncionalidad de la agricultura familiar y adaptación al cambio climático en los Andes colombianos" ;
    nex:url "https://www.mundoagrario.unlp.edu.ar/"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/128963> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 128963 ;
    nex:description "Este texto presenta la reseña del libro Injusticia sin fin: La brecha pensional de género e ideas para cerrarla, editado por Laura Porras-Santanilla y Natalia Ramírez-Bustamante. A lo largo del texto, sostengo que el libro contribuye a documentar un fenómeno clave que ha sido poco desarrollado en Colombia: la doble brecha pensional de género. Para ello, presento la agenda de investigación previa que llevó a la publicación del libro, sus principales hallazgos y las líneas de investigación que abre. También relaciono los hallazgos con una de sus principales causas: la distribución injusta de las cargas de cuidado." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/75650> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2024 ;
    nex:title "Injusticia sin fin: La brecha pensional de género e ideas para cerrarla" ;
    nex:url "https://www.icesi.edu.co/revistas/index.php/precedente/article/view/7228"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/128978> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 128978 ;
    nex:classification "A" ;
    nex:description "Inverted perovskite solar cells (IPSC) represent a promising alternative for photovoltaic energy generation due to their high power conversion efficiency (PCE). Their fabrication makes these devices a cost-effective option with significant potential for solar energy generation. Nickel oxide (NiOx) has been investigated as a hole-transport layer material in these IPSCs due to its high electrical conductivity and its influence on PCE stability. Despite previous reports, there are opportunities for improvement in the NiOx/Perovskite interface, which are key aspects for device performance. This study evaluated the effect of fluoride surface treatment on electrochemically deposited (ECD) NiOx from two concentrations of an aqueous solution of NH4F, performed via spin-coating, on the properties and reproducibility of IPSCs. The highest efficiency was achieved under the NiOx-F 1 mg mL⁻¹ condition, reaching a PCE of 19.12 % compared to the reference NiOx which showed a PCE of 17.32 %. This research offers new insights and delves into the reasons behind these improvements, showing through electrochemical analysis and series resistance studies that the probable causes include better charge conduction and high recombination resistance at the interface. Finally, the perovskite grain sizes on NiOx-ECD were larger than those reported in the literature with colloidal NiOx, contributing to greater device stability." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/7918> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2025 ;
    nex:title "Effect of NH4F surface treatment of electrodeposited NiOx on the properties and reproducibility of inverted perovskite solar cells" ;
    nex:url "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2468023024018091"^^xsd:anyURI .

