<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/131140> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 131140 ;
    nex:classification "C" ;
    nex:description "Este artículo reúne lecciones y reflexiones de la experiencia de 4 versiones de curso entre 2022 y 2023, donde, junto a la profesora Mónica Sánchez Bernal dictamos la Unidad de Profundización “Arquitectura con enfoque de género y diferencial. “La inaplazable incorporación del enfoque de género en la enseñanza de la arquitectura del siglo XXI”, plasma nuestra convicción en pro de una educación en arquitectura más incluyente y sensible al género, con soluciones espaciales conscientes de su potencial impacto." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/7399> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2025 ;
    nex:title "La inaplazable incorporación del enfoque de género en la enseñanza de la arquitectura del siglo XXI" ;
    nex:url "https://doi.org/10.18389/dearq41.2025.03"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/131145> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 131145 ;
    nex:classification "B" ;
    nex:description "The Logarithmic Mean Divisia Index (LMDI) decomposition analysis is widely used to examine carbon dioxide emissions related to energy consumption. This study replicates previous findings by applying a novel multi-period methodology to define the time frame for decomposition analysis. The methodology overcomes limitations in traditional approaches by accounting for trend changes in the time series. The proposed technique minimizes total mean squared error (TMSE) using linear models. The results, along with computational performance tests, demonstrate that this method effectively identifies optimal partitions, making it well-suited for annualized case studies on carbon dioxide emission decomposition." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/43324> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2025 ;
    nex:title "Assessing Computational Complexity in Selecting Periods for LMDI Techniques in Energy-Related Carbon Dioxide Emissions: An Alternative Approach" ;
    nex:url "https://doi.org/10.1002/ese3.70187"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/131166> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 131166 ;
    nex:classification "A" ;
    nex:description "This short paper describes an efficient method for Optimal Coordination of Directional Over-Current Protections (OC-DOCP) considering Sequential Trips at Both Line-Ends (ST-BLE) and selectivity for all Fault Locations (FLs). The first step is a basic OC-DOCP solution with only close-in faults. The second step is an assessment of the previous solution, considering ST-BLE, to find the FL with the worst loss of selectivity for each pair main-backup. The third step is an OC-DOCP solution considering ST-BLE and the constraints related to the found FLs. The second and third steps are iteratively repeated until a given selectivity level is reached. Results were computed for a recognized test case, using the three standardized IEC curve types. For the analyzed case, which considers phase overcurrent functions and three-phase faults, the proposed method reaches the same results as the available alternative, recently published, and the proposed method is 14.2 times faster and requires a number of iterations 3.7 times lower" ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/43324> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2025 ;
    nex:title "An efficient method for optimal coordination of directional overcurrent protections considering transient configurations and all possible fault locations" ;
    nex:url "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.compeleceng.2025.110554"^^xsd:anyURI .

