<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/134781> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 134781 ;
    nex:classification "C" ;
    nex:description "Este artículo realiza un análisis de la trayectoria académica y los aportes intelectuales de Luz Gabriela Arango, reconocida socióloga colombiana. En las 65 publicaciones revisadas, entre artículos, capítulos de  libro  y  libros  en  sus  tres  décadas  de  producción  intelectual,  desde  1991 hasta 20181, se sintetizan algunos elementos del legado académico, en tres grandes temáticas que, si bien no son estrictamente cronológicas, reflejan el devenir de algunas de  las  discusiones  que  los  distintos  congresos  académicos, especialmente de la Asociación Latinoamericana de Estudios del Trabajo ALAST." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/9834> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2025 ;
    nex:title "Luz  Gabriela  Arango:  un  legado  intelectual  feminista" ;
    nex:url "https://revistas.unal.edu.co/index.php/recs"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/134782> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 134782 ;
    nex:description "Las trayectorias educativas constituyen un  foco  fundamental  para  comprender  los  desafíos,  tensiones  y  oportunidades  que  enfrentan  estudiantes  y  docentes  a  lo largo de su vida escolar. Su análisis y re-flexión permite identificar y valorar algu-nos de los puntos críticos en el recorrido formativo de muchas personas." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/43314> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2025 ;
    nex:title "Trayectorias educativas: contextos, retos y perspectivas" ;
    nex:url "https://revistas.idep.edu.co/index.php/educacion-y-ciudad/article/view/3479/2526"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/134783> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 134783 ;
    nex:description "Details on fatty acid and lipid metabolism in Malassezia spp. are limited, amongst others, because efficient growth of Malassezia spp. in defined media with free fatty acids has not yet been described. Here, we describe a culturing method in a defined medium in which lipid-dependent growth of Malassezia spp. can be studied. We observed efficient growth of Malassezia furfur and Malassezia pachydermatis in liquid minimal medium supplemented with palmitic acid in the presence of NP-40 Tergitol™. We introduced a 3-day fatty acid-starvation phase to reduce residual growth due to the carry-over of lipids from rich media. The Malassezia spp. studied remained viable longer in liquid media lacking fatty acids and detergents, as described previously for a Saccharomyces cerevisiae fas1 mutant. This suggests that Malassezia spp. might have developed mechanisms to survive periods of fatty acid starvation. We compared the lipidome of both Malassezia species grown in mDixon or a defined medium with NP-40 Tergitol™ supplemented with either palmitate and/or oleic acid, or ox bile. Remarkably, the lipidome of mDixon grown cells is enriched in lipid species associated with lipid droplets. Malassezia spp. adapt their lipid composition after growth in a defined medium, and a subset of novel lipid species was identified." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/7806> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2025 ;
    nex:title "Lipid-dependent growth of Malassezia spp. in defined medium with single fatty acids" ;
    nex:url "https://academic.oup.com/femsyr/article/doi/10.1093/femsyr/foaf043/8239275"^^xsd:anyURI .

