<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/135150> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 135150 ;
    nex:description """Gastrosonics explores how our consumer experiences with taste and smell modulate our creative activities and how musical phenomena impact the gastronomic industry. This is an emergent research field within the framework of applied music production. In this article we discuss musicological, creative, human-food interaction, as well as marketing strategies toward an enhanced interdisciplinary dialogue. We also introduce a rationale of sonic seasoning as scientific support for gastrosonic practice (a field where co-author, and marketing professor, Felipe Reinoso-Carvalho is a renowned reference). We further document a gastrosonics pilot study involving 12 consumers doing asynchronous musical activities in domestic settings. The activities involved sound mixing using the SoundSphere ecology while drinking different products such as coffee, water, and orange, lemon and apple juice. We finish by discussing the limitations related to existing support infrastructure and the requisites and potentialities for future similar assessments. Importantly, this is part of a strategy led by prof. Felipe Reinoso-Carvalho that intends to disseminate this kind of knowledge beyond the English language. As such, this is the first scientific article where this professor decides to focus on a portuguese-speaking audience and, therefore, the entire article has been written in portugues and purposely published in an outlet that welcomes this kind of research (namely Musica Hodie). This journal’s aims to disseminate and share original research freely within the academic community, focusing on themes related to interdiscilpinary research lines involving the application of music into other scopes, such as marketing. Recent articles related to marketing published by this journal includes: 

Pérez-Rufi, J. P., Martín-Martín, P., Pérez-Rufi, M. I. (2025). Postdigital Music Marketing in the Brat Era of Charli XCX: Identity, Transmedia Storytelling and Cultural Phenomenon. Musica Hodie . DOI: https://doi.org/10.5216/mh.v25.82367""" ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/51449> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2025 ;
    nex:title "Tasteful Music: An exploratory analysis of gastrosonics using the SoundSphere ecology" ;
    nex:url "https://revistas.ufg.br/musica/article/view/80249/43796"^^xsd:anyURI .

