<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/137512> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 137512 ;
    nex:description "A wide range of informal and shared transport services, including shared taxis, minivans, motorcycle taxis, and bicycle taxis, plays a growing role in Bogotá's mobility system. These services provide flexible travel alternatives for underserved communities, but they operate with varying levels of governance, regulation, and integration. Some modes have developed semiformal organizational arrangements, while others remain in regulatory limbo, facing limited recognition in transport planning, road safety concerns, conflicts with formal public transport, and vulnerability to policy changes. This paper presents the Bogotá Informal and Shared Mobility Living Lab, a participatory urban initiative designed to engage transport operators, communities, and policymakers in jointly developing experimental solutions. The study focuses on the Lab's design and methodological framework rather than on the implementation or evaluation of pilot interventions. Guided by a Theory of Change approach, the Lab established a structured framework to support collaborative problem-solving and adaptive policymaking. The methodology is based on a participatory diagnosis that included six focus groups with 48 participants across three geographic case areas. Through an iterative process of diagnosis, thematic discussions, and co-creation of intervention pathways, the Lab defined its mission and vision and established the organizational structure of local teams. These teams are intended to support future experimentation in contexts where shared mobility systems operate under diverse regulatory and community conditions. By placing participatory research, governance adaptation, and knowledge co-production at its core, the Lab offers a scalable approach for engaging informal transport providers. The findings show how such initiatives can function as platforms for testing alternative governance models, fostering intersectoral collaboration, and integrating informal mobility into broader urban sustainability strategies. Although implementation remains for future work, this paper documents the methodology underlying the Lab and highlights its potential to inform policy innovation and promote more inclusive governance of shared transport systems." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/8636> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2026 ;
    nex:title "From diagnosis to action: A theory of change framework for informal and shared mobility in Bogotá" ;
    nex:url "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0966692326001547"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/137516> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 137516 ;
    nex:classification "B" ;
    nex:description "Este artículo busca aportar a la comprensión de lo que ocurre en la brecha entre las reglas jurídicas y la realidad. Esto, con dos objetivos: por un lado, mostrar algunos de los imaginarios legales replicados por la academia colombiana y, por otro, plantear cómo usar metodologías no tradicionales en la enseñanza legal aporta a desimaginarlos o reflexionar sobre ellos. Los tres imaginarios elegidos provienen de la dogmática del derecho administrativo: i) que la operación del derecho atiende exclusivamente al contenido reglado, ii) que únicamente los agentes estatales producen decisiones jurídicas y iii) que las emociones de los operadores del derecho no influyen en la decisión legal. La utilización de metodologías pedagógicas como cuentos y materiales audiovisuales permiten desimaginar estos imaginarios. El artículo concluye proponiendo una agenda de investigación y de pedagogía jurídica que resalta el aporte que la utilización de estas metodologías tiene para la comprensión de aspectos subteorizados en la disciplina legal." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/75650> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2025 ;
    nex:title "Desimaginando imaginarios legales a través del uso de contenido audiovisual en clase" ;
    nex:url "https://pedagogiaderecho.uchile.cl/index.php/RPUD/article/view/77200"^^xsd:anyURI .

