<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/138169> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 138169 ;
    nex:description "Lipid oxidation is a major factor limiting the shelf-life and quality of pork burgers, promoting physicochemical and sensory deterioration during storage. This study evaluated the effect of microencapsulated Sacha inchi oil (SIE) as a functional lipid replacer on the oxidative stability and technological properties of pork burgers under refrigerated conditions. Four formulations were developed: a control (without SIE) and three treatments with partial replacement of pork backfat by 0.5%, 1.0%, and 1.5% SIE. Samples were stored for 21 days and analyzed for pH, color (L*, a*, b*), texture, juiciness, cooking loss, shrinkage, total phenolic content, antioxidant capacity, and lipid oxidation (TBARS). A two-way ANOVA was used to determine the effect of SIE concentration and storage time on quality parameters. SIE incorporation and storage time significantly affected (p ≤ 0.05) key technological parameters, increasing redness (a*), juiciness, and hardness by up to 62.78%, 57.46%, and 59.49%, respectively. Additionally, SIE enhanced water-holding capacity, resulting in reduced cooking loss, improved structural integrity, and a fresher visual appearance. Despite the presence of bioactive compounds, lipid oxidation increased with higher SIE concentrations and storage time (53.06–69.99 µg MDA/kg), indicating that encapsulation provided limited protection against oxidative degradation under the evaluated conditions. In conclusion, microencapsulated Sacha inchi oil is a promising ingredient for improving technological performance and quality attributes of pork burgers, although it does not confer oxidative stability during storage." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/60561> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2026 ;
    nex:title "Effect of microencapsulated Sacha inchi oil on technological quality and oxidative stability of pork burgers during refrigerated storage" ;
    nex:url "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S2949824426003368"^^xsd:anyURI .

