<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/138397> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 138397 ;
    nex:description """Intentions play at least three roles in our psychological life: helping us think about the future, shaping our deliberation
concerning what to do, and guiding us in doing what we do. This paper focuses mainly on the latter, also known
under the head of intention in action. I discuss specific assumptions, such as that intentions represent states of
affairs as the result of actions and that it is precisely in virtue of performing such a representational function that
they can guide us in acting. I argue that representational assumptions have problematic consequences concerning
how both actions and their results relate to time. To avoid such difficulties, I offer a nonrepresentational and
ecologically based explanation of the guiding role of intention.""" ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/7295> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2026 ;
    nex:title "Intention, experience, and history. An ecological approach" ;
    nex:url "https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/09515089.2026.2701795"^^xsd:anyURI .

