<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/138825> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 138825 ;
    nex:description "A new series of chalcone-appended 9-styryldihydroacridinone molecular hybrids was synthesized through a straightforward two-step sequence involving Friedländer annulation followed by Claisen–Schmidt condensation. This molecular hybridization strategy integrates the acridinone scaffold with styryl and chalcone pharmacophoric motifs within a single molecular framework, affording structurally diverse compounds of potential interest in medicinal chemistry and diversity-oriented heterocyclic synthesis. The target compounds were obtained in moderate to good yields and comprehensively characterized by FT-IR, HRMS, NMR, and single-crystal X-ray diffraction analyses of selected representatives. Crystallographic studies confirmed the exclusive formation of the E-configured benzylidene derivatives and revealed that their molecular conformations are primarily governed by the puckering of the cyclohexenone ring and the non-coplanar arrangement of the aromatic moieties. Electrostatic potential mapping combined with Hirshfeld surface analysis demonstrated that the crystal packing is predominantly stabilized by weak non-classical intermolecular interactions, particularly C−H‧‧‧O hydrogen bonds, while dispersive H‧‧‧H and C-H‧‧‧π contacts represent the major contributions to the overall intermolecular interaction landscape. Four representative molecular hybrids were further evaluated for antiproliferative activity against the NCI-60 human tumor cell line panel at a single concentration of 10 μM. However, none of the compounds met the NCI criteria for progression to the five-dose screening stage. Although no significant antiproliferative activity was observed, the synthesized hybrids represent valuable synthetic intermediates owing to the presence of a highly reactive α,β-unsaturated carbonyl functionality, which provides a versatile platform for the construction of structurally more complex fused benzoheterocyclic derivatives." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/43204> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2027 ;
    nex:title "Novel Functionalized Chalcone-Appended Styryldihydroacridinone Molecular Hybrids: Synthesis, Spectroscopic Characterization, and Crystallographic Insights from ESP and Hirshfeld Surface Analysis" ;
    nex:url "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0022286026022994"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/138830> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 138830 ;
    nex:description "Systematic review of 293 Scopus and Web of Science publications (2004-2025) on conversational agents and brand relationships, combining bibliometric analysis, topic modelling with language models and an expert-AI validation protocol. The study identifies five thematic clusters (functional competence, social simulation, anthropomorphic projection, technological affordances and emotional resonance) and proposes the Signals-Mechanisms-Outcomes (SMO) framework, which links configurable agent design features to psychological mediators and brand relationship outcomes. It defines three boundary tensions: the anthropomorphism paradox, the stage-contingency problem and the intensity asymmetry between positive and negative outcomes." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/99922> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2026 ;
    nex:title "Brand relationships in conversation: a review of conversational agents using bibliometrics and language models" ;
    nex:url "https://doi.org/10.1108/JPBM-02-2025-5785"^^xsd:anyURI .

