<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/51857> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 51857 ;
    nex:classification "A" ;
    nex:description """Pompe disease is a recessive autosomic disease caused by intramuscular storage of lysosomal glycogen. This is caused by a genetic alteration that causes an alpha glucosidase deficiency. Phenotypic expression of the disease includes proximal progressive myopathy, increased CK and respiratory alterations among others. Diagnostic of Pompe disease includes assessment of Alpha Glucosidase activities in at least two different tissues. Usually, the process starts with a DBS screening test in patients with clinical manifestations or high-risk populations and subsequent confirmatory tests on leucocytes or other tissue samples. 
Confirmatory tests in leucocytes are an easy way to assess enzymatic activity values, due to its easily isolation. Nevertheless, could have non-conclusive or borderline results mainly caused by enzyme isoforms degrading artificial substrate used in the technique. Based on a modification of the previous techniques described by Shapira, Reuser and Vandiggelen, we demonstrate here the results of a four-year Colombian experience.""" ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/10773> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2018 ;
    nex:title "Confirmatory assays for alpha-glucosidase enzymatic values using glycogen: An improving test for the diagnosis of Pompe disease" ;
    nex:url "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/322964313_Confirmatory_assays_for_alpha-glucosidase_enzymatic_values_using_glycogen_An_improving_test_for_the_diagnosis_of_Pompe_disease"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/51858> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 51858 ;
    nex:classification "A" ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/10773> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2018 ;
    nex:title "Genetic and enzymatic studies in a cluster of mucopolysaccharidosis type I patients in northwest Colombia" ;
    nex:url "http://doi.org/10.1016/j.ymgme.2017.12.376"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/51859> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 51859 ;
    nex:classification "A" ;
    nex:description "Internal quality assurance procedures have been stablished to detect, reduce and correct, possible analytical deficiencies before submitting results on which a therapeutic conduct relies. From its implementation on clinical laboratories there has been an increased necessity to extend his efforts to other facilities as for example, investigational centers.  Reference centers for enzymatic assays do not have commercial controls which helps to validate its results. This issue, engender internally the need to prepare normal or abnormal controls databases for following of diagnostic assays, trying to establish performance traits as variability coefficients, intra-essay coefficients, inter-essay coefficients, standard deviation and measure ranges among others.  We present the internal quality assurance process on DBS activity values, in control samples for Beta-galactosidase(BG), Total Hexosaminidase (TH) and Alpha-galactosidase A (AG) using 1,2 mm punchs. (duplicated). The measurement of activities was realized using final point fluorometric assays on artificial substrates marked with 4-methylumbelliferone. Equipment: Spectramax M2(Molecular Devices Corp.)" ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/10773> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2018 ;
    nex:title "Implementation of internal quality control for the determination of the activity of lysosomal enzymes in dried blood samples" ;
    nex:url "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/322970798_Implementation_of_internal_quality_control_for_the_determination_of_the_activity_of_lysosomal_enzymes_in_dried_blood_samples"^^xsd:anyURI .

