<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/64650> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 64650 ;
    nex:classification "A" ;
    nex:description "The ethnic and rural communities´ processes in defence of their territory present a complex and urgent challenge in the Colombian context. Once again it exhibits its difficulties after the long peace process that culminated with the 2016 Havana Accords. With the uncertainties of the current post-conflict scenario, regulations and framework initiatives have generated an important debate that affects community life projects. The particular complexity of the Caribbean region involves ethnic claims historically located in the Montes de María, a place of permanent social struggle, where the armed conflict provoked intense forced-displacement dynamics.   This research encompasses the collective processes of territorial affirmation of the Afro-Colombian and rural communities. It investigates the scope and impact capacity of the formulation and development of the Afro-Colombian community councils life plans as effective governance mechanisms that allow communities to remain in the territory with dignity. Based on Participatory Action Research -PAR-, this work shows proposals and collective narratives that allow the construction of the territory from a differential approach and that generate social renewal in the Afro-Colombian and rural communities of the Colombian Caribbean region. It aims to provide meaning to a new proposal of the social construction of the habitat where to inhabit is not only to reside, to be within, or to occupy a space. It is to provide our time and space with everyday meaning." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/27301> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2024 ;
    nex:title "ETHNODEVELOPMENT AND POST-CONFLICT: New challenges for the social construction of habitat with territorial justice in the Afro-Colombian Caribbean" ;
    nex:url "https://doi.org/10.1080/17442222.2024.2413230"^^xsd:anyURI .

