<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/74027> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 74027 ;
    nex:classification "B" ;
    nex:description "© 2021, The Author(s), under exclusive licence to Springer-Verlag GmbH, AT part of Springer Nature.Bacteriophages are considered the most abundant biological entities on earth, and they are able to modulate the populations of their bacterial hosts. Although the potential of bacteriophages has been accepted as an alternative strategy to combat multidrug-resistant pathogenic bacteria, there still exists a considerable knowledge gap regarding their genetic diversity, which hinders their use as antimicrobial agents. In this study, we undertook a genomic and phylogenetic characterization of the phage Ab11510-phi, which was isolated from a multidrug-resistant Acinetobacter baumannii strain (Ab11510). We found that Ab11510-phi has a narrow host range and belongs to a small group of transposable phages of the genus Vieuvirus that have only been reported to infect Acinetobacter bacteria. Finally, we showed that Ab11510-phi (as well as other vieuvirus phages) has a high level of mosaicism. On a broader level, we demonstrate that comparative genomics and phylogenetic analysis are necessary tools for the proper characterization of phage diversity." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/10094> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2021 ;
    nex:title "A novel vieuvirus from multidrug-resistant Acinetobacter baumannii" ;
    nex:url "http://doi.org/10.1007/s00705-021-05010-4"^^xsd:anyURI .

