<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/80839> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 80839 ;
    nex:classification "D" ;
    nex:description "We studied how specialized advisors impact the implementation of good corporate governance practices at the firm and family level. We follow a qualitative case study approach using 4 cases in 4 different industries with diverse levels of management sophistication. We show that not only the firms’ governance structures output, such as board of directors and general shareholder meetings, but also the family governance output, such as family protocols and family councils, substantially improved with the advisors’ intervention. We highlight the seldom studied in the academic literature but important role of advisors not only in the design of better governance structure at the business and family level, but also in its implementation. We also highlight the importance of building confidence, transparency, and trust, between the advisor and the family." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/8532> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2021 ;
    nex:title "Advisors in Corporate Governance of Family Firms" .

