<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/87735> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 87735 ;
    nex:classification "A" ;
    nex:description "This article addresses the causes of the virtual disintegration of the Union of South American Nations (UNASUR) from the perspective of analytical eclecticism. It is part of crescent literature around the debate on International Relations theory end, in which analytical eclecticism and integrative pluralism emerge as viable but contested explanative strategies. The study of UNASUR and its fate has been prolific. In it, rival explanations such as neoclassical realism, institutional liberalism, and social-constructivism have been dominant. Although each approach can highlight essential angles on the multifactorial causes of the end of the most ambitious South American organization, we consider that their explanatory powers are limited. Thus, we start from analytical eclecticism and sequentially analyze UNASUR from neoclassical realism, institutional liberalism, and social-constructivism to comprehensively explain the case." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/53752> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2022 ;
    nex:title "UNASUR: An eclectic analytical perspective of its disintegration" ;
    nex:url "http://doi.org/10.7440/colombiaint111.2022.04"^^xsd:anyURI .

