<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/126635> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 126635 ;
    nex:classification "C" ;
    nex:description "The initial years of the Economics Department and the Center for the Study of Development Economics at Universidad de los Andes are an exemplary case of the beginnings of the formation of professional economists in Colombia. Through archival research we reconstruct the first twenty years of this project that counted with the support of the Rockefeller Foundation and answered to the increasing demand for professional economists capable of producing technical analysis of the countries development challenges." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/7089>,
        <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/8756> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2019 ;
    nex:title "Becoming a pragmatic technocrat. The beginnings of professional training of colombian economists" ;
    nex:url "https://api.elsevier.com/content/abstract/scopus_id/85067811628"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/126643> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 126643 ;
    nex:classification "A" ;
    nex:description "To evaluate the capabilities of RoofClassify in the Colombian context, we propose applying the methodology developed by Tomassini et al. in the urban center of Sibaté, located in the department of Cundinamarca, Colombia. There are two primary reasons for selecting this site. Firstly, Sibaté is the focus of a comprehensive study aiming to characterize the entire asbestos exposome following the discovery of the first mesothelioma cluster in Colombia [34] and the identification of friable asbestos in the municipality's subsoil [35]. Therefore, conducting the evaluation in Sibaté aligns with the broader research effort focused on understanding asbestos-related risks in the region. Secondly, the topographical characteristics of the city, with its elevated points, facilitate direct roof identification. This aspect is of utmost importance both for establishing the training layers required for the analysis and for evaluating the performance of the RoofClassify plugin. By conducting the evaluation in Sibaté, we aim to assess the effectiveness and adaptability of the RoofClassify plugin in Colombia with specific environmental and contextual factors that differ from the original study." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/10015>,
        <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/31148> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2024 ;
    nex:title "Remote Detection of Asbestos-Cement Roofs: Evaluating a QGIS Plugin in a low- and middle-income country" ;
    nex:url "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2352938524002155"^^xsd:anyURI .

