<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/24112> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 24112 ;
    nex:classification "A" ;
    nex:description "Chitotriosidase as a biomarker for the diagnostic approach of lysosomal storage disorders in Colombia Pacheco, N. & Uribe, A. Lysosomal storage disorders (LSDs) are a group of pathologies that enclose the damage of an enzyme and its pathological consequences due to the accumulation of substrate in the lysosomes. In Colombia, these entities are misdiagnosed because many of them are not widely known. A biomarker is defined as a molecule that works as an indicator of disease, being a useful tool for the diagnostic approach." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/10773>,
