<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/75176> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 75176 ;
    nex:description "Population games can be regarded as a tool to study the strategic interaction of a population of players. Although several attention has been given to such field, most of the available works have focused only on the unconstrained case. That is, the allowed equilibrium of the game is not constrained. To further extend the capabilities of population games, in this paper we propose a novel class of primal-dual evolutionary dynamics that allow the consideration of constraints that must be satisfied at the equilibrium of the game. Using duality theory and Lyapunov stability theory, we provide sufficient conditions to guarantee the asymptotic stability and feasibility of the equilibria set of the game under the considered constraints. Furthermore, we illustrate the application of the developed theory to some classical population games with the addition of constraints." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/52045>,
        <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/9944> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2020 ;
    nex:title "Primal-dual evolutionary dynamics for constrained population games" .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/75197> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 75197 ;
    nex:classification "A" ;
    nex:description "Pre-exposure prophylaxis (PrEP) has limited availability across Latin America, though access is increasing. We explored PrEP uptake in Mexico via an online survey completed by Spanish-speaking, Hornet geosocial networking application (GSN app) users without HIV (n = 2020). Most (81.3%) had heard of PrEP, 3.5% were current users, and 34.2% intended to take PrEP within six months. Current PrEP use was associated with PrEP eligibility (aOR 26.07 [95%CI 13.05–52.09], p < 0.001), recent STI testing (aOR 3.79 [95%CI 1.10–13.11], p = 0.035), and recent chemsex (aOR 3.02 [95%CI 1.02–8.93], p = 0.046). Recent STI testing was associated with hearing about PrEP from a doctor (aOR 3.26 [95%CI 1.98–5.36], p < 0.001), and those who lived in large cities were less likely to have learned about PrEP via Hornet (aOR 0.52 [95%CI 0.32–0.85], p = 0.009). Interventions to increase PrEP uptake in Mexico should build upon existing health networks and utilize GSN apps for PrEP information dissemination, particularly in less populated areas." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/10154>,
        <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/46245> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2021 ;
    nex:title "PrEP Awareness, Use, Intention to Use, and Information Source Among Geosocial Networking Application Users in Mexico in 2018–2019" ;
    nex:url "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10461-021-03184-1"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/75198> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 75198 ;
    nex:classification "A" ;
    nex:description """As an envisioned technology for future smart city-networks, this paper studies the decentralized charging coordination of a fleet of plug-in electric vehicles (PEVs). In particular, we explore some recent ideas in the fields of population games and payoff dynamics models, and we propose a set of continuous-time optimization dynamics for the charging coordination of PEVs in smart city-networks. The proposed method is able to coordinate the charging profiles of multiple PEVs in a decentralized fashion under a general convex objective, and guarantees the satisfaction of hard operational constraints on the power capacities of the charging ports of the PEVs and the feeder lines of
the distribution network. The stability of the proposed method is investigated through nonlinear Lyapunov analysis, and is validated through numerical simulations considering a fleet with several PEVs.""" ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/52045>,
        <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/9944> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2022 ;
    nex:title "Decentralized Charging Coordination of Electric Vehicles: A Payoff Dynamics Model Approach" ;
    nex:url "http://doi.org/10.1109/TCNS.2021.3128498"^^xsd:anyURI .

<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/75199> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 75199 ;
    nex:classification "A" ;
    nex:description """This brief proposes a novel form of continuous-time evolutionary game dynamics for (generalized) Nash equilibrium seeking in equality-constrained population games. Using Lyapunov stability theory and duality theory, we provide sufficient conditions to guarantee the stability, non-emptiness, compactness, and optimality of the equilibria
set of the proposed dynamics for certain classes of population games. In addition, we illustrate our theoretical developments through a numerical simulation of an equality-constrained congestion game.""" ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/52045>,
        <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/9944> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2022 ;
    nex:title "A Payoff Dynamics Model for Equality-Constrained Population Games" ;
    nex:url "http://doi.org/10.1109/LCSYS.2021.3082865"^^xsd:anyURI .

