<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/75916> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 75916 ;
    nex:description """Article accepted in Theoretical Economic Letters

We build a theoretical model of demand-driven structural change where individuals have different endowments of productive factors. These differences
in endowments generate income inequality. The main result is that for economies with a low factor endowment (poor economies), an increase in inequality can accelerate structural change.""" ;
