<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/76216> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 76216 ;
    nex:classification "A" ;
    nex:description "This paper addresses the first photogrammetry reconstruction of Ciudad Antigua, a pre-Hispanic archaeological site in Sierra Nevada de Santa Marta, Colombia. It is derived from a project where visualization and computation techniques applied to vestiges of cultural value can contribute to social appropriation and protection of these ancient settlements. The construction characteristics and symbolic relevance of places such as Ciudad Antigua, constitute a major part of the country's cultural heritage. However, the remote location and little knowledge of these places, on behalf of the general population, are a disadvantage for their protection and conservation. By means of research as the one presented here, archaeological sites like Ciudad Antigua can be made more accessible in a virtual sense, while contributing to greater empathy and shared responsibility in society. This paper engages in a broader discussion of the computational reconstruction of archaeological sites with cultural relevance, looking into a comprehensive model to understand the relationship between physical sites, digital representation, computational simulation, and algorithmic analysis." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/7524>,
        <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/9178> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2021 ;
    nex:title "Ciudad Antigua: From Remote Sensing to Virtual Interactive Experience of a Pre-Hispanic Settlement in Colombia" ;
    nex:url "http://doi.org/10.7238/a. v0i28.375755"^^xsd:anyURI .

