<https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/article/99335> a nex:JournalArticle ;
    nex:articleId 99335 ;
    nex:classification "B" ;
    nex:description "Developing analytical methods to quantify ethanol extant in liqueurs and hydrocarbons is crucial. Herein, we report the first example of a solvatofluorochromic molecular probe to rapid ethanol sensing in distilled spirits after a simple liquid-liquid extraction. The molecule consists of a hybrid 2-(4-nitrophenyl)pyrazo lo [1,5-a]pyrimidine–triphenylamine compound (TP) with a robust push-pull effect. The probe acted linearly responded to ethanol in the concentration range from 10 to 50 %vol and was applied in the accurate EtOH determination in whiskey, tequila, rum, and aguardiente. The photophysical behavior of TP was interpreted in terms of dipolarity (SdP) and acidity of the solvent (SA). Besides, the TP crystal structure was studied by X-ray diffraction, managing to find a correlation between emission spectra in the solid-state (λem = 583 nm) and the supramolecular structure. This final study suggests that the emission of TP is mainly related to molecular effects, in this case, an intramolecular charge transfer (ICT) from a triphenylamine moiety to a nitro group (TPA → NO2)." ;
    nex:hasAuthor <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/43204>,
        <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/55505>,
        <https://w3id.org/nexus/resource/professor/9890> ;
    nex:productType "article" ;
    nex:publicationYear 2022 ;
    nex:title "Expeditious ethanol quantification present in hydrocarbons and distilled spirits: Extending photophysical usages of the pyrazolo[1,5-a]pyrimidines" ;
    nex:url "http://doi.org/10.1016/j.dyepig.2022.110299"^^xsd:anyURI .

