√
s
=
13
 
 
TeV
, corresponding to an integrated luminosity of 
137
 
 
fb
−
1
, recorded with the CMS detector. The coupling strength with respect to the standard model value, 
Y
t
, is determined from kinematic distributions in 
t
¯
t
 final states containing 
e
e
, 
μ
μ
, or 
e
μ
 pairs. Variations of the Yukawa coupling strength lead to modified distributions for 
t
¯
t
 production. In particular, the distributions of the mass of the 
t
¯
t
 system and the rapidity difference of the top quark and antiquark are sensitive to the value of 
